THE DEEPER BLOCKER: there is no one to kill. `search_game_tree` on the Server datamodel during this
same ACTIVE phase found exactly one entry under `Players` (`Players.Demiurgos_18`), and both
`Workspace.Corpses` and `Workspace.Husks` exist as folders with zero children. `RoundService`'s
`dealtInUserIds()` only draws UserIds from `state.PlayerStates`, which is populated only by real
connected Players (src/server/Services/RoundService.luau:599-611) — `ForceAswangWhenSolo` changes
*which* candidate is picked as Aswang, it does not add a second candidate. With one candidate forced
to Aswang, the round has zero survivors and zero husks; a husk is only created when a connected
Player disconnects or idles out mid-round (RoundService.luau ~1051-1061), which itself requires a
second Player to have been connected in the first place.

Net effect: `RequestKill` has no valid TargetUserId to send in this session, in any phase, no matter
how long the round runs. `beginFeed` (MonsterService.luau:1278) is reachable only from `commitKill`,
which is reachable only from a kill that actually validated against a live target or husk
(`validateAndKill` / `validateAndKillHusk`) — neither exists here. This is true for all seven
questions, not just the new one: none of them can be produced with exactly one Studio client
connected, regardless of Config.

